// error: `Half` derives `Eq` without `Hash`; equal instances must hash alike, so derive both: `derives Eq, Hash`
// error: `Hashed` derives `Hash` without `Eq`; the hash follows the fields `==` compares, so derive both: `derives Eq, Hash`
// error: `Sorted` derives `Ord` without `Eq`; ordering by the fields needs `==` by the same fields, so derive `Eq, Hash` with it
class Half(n: int) derives Eq

class Hashed(n: int) derives Hash

class Sorted(n: int) derives Ord

main()
  println(1)
